{"id":"word:hebrew:H4975","type":"word","title":"מֹתֶן","subtitle":"H4975 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, the waist or small of the back; only in plural the loins","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מֹתֶן (H4975) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 47 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מֹתֶן (môthen) means properly, the waist or small of the back; only in plural the loins First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 2 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מֹתֶן","transliteration":"môthen","pronunciation":"mo'-then","strong":"H4975","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4975","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בְּ/מָתְנָ֑י/ו","בְּ/מָתְנָ֔י/ו","מִ/מָּתְנֵ֥י","מָתְנָ֑י/ו","מָתְנֶ֗י/ךָ"],"morphs":[["HNcmda",9],["HR/Ncmdc/Sp3ms",7],["HNcmdc/Sp3ms",7],["HNcmdc/Sp2ms",6],["HR/Ncmdc/Sp3mp",3],["HR/Ncmdc",2],["HR/Ncmdc/Sp1cp",2],["HNcmdc/Sp1cs",2],["HC/Ncmdc/Sp3ms",1],["HNcmdc/Sp2mp",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, the waist or small of the back; only in plural the loins","usage":"greyhound, loins, side.","full":"H4975. mothen מָתְנַ֫יִם noun masculine dual loins (Arabic back , the two sides of the back , etc.; Syriac ; — absolute ׳מ Deut 33:11 7 t., מָתְנָ֑יִם Ezek 29:7 ; 47:4 ; construct מָתְנֵי Jer 13:11 + 3t.; suffix מָתְנַי Isa 21:3 , מָתְנָ֑י Jer 13:2 ; מָתְנֵיהֶם 1Kings + Jeremiah 20:32 4 t., etc.; — loins: 1. a. place of wearing girdle 1Kin 2:5 ; 2Kin 1:8 ; Jer 13:1-2 , 4 , 11 ; Ezek 23:15 ; figurative Isa 11:5 righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins . b. hence place of things attached to girdle: — sword girded on ( אסר על, חגר 2Sam 20:8 ; Neh 4:12 ; opposed to, אֲפַתֵּחַ מְלָכִים וּמָתְנֵי Isa 45:1 and the loins of kings I will loosen , i e. will disarm them ( ׳י before Cyrus; compare Che); ink-horn Ezek 9:2-3 , 11 . c. girding up loins = make ready for action, מָתְנָיו וַיְשַׁנֵּס 1Kin 18:46 ; more often מ ׳חָגַר 2Kin 4:29 ; 9:1 ; Exod 12:11 (P), Dan 10:5 ; מ ׳אָזַר Jer 1:17 . d. מ ׳זַרְזִיר Prov 30:31 that which is girt in the loins , i.e. probably either a greyhound Ew Bö De (contracted, as if by a belt), or a war-horse, charger, Bo Ges Hi Str Wild (with a saddle); compare also זרזיר , p. 267 above; text perhaps corrupt (Wild). e. girded with sackcloth (in mourning) Gen 37:34 (J), Amos 8:10 ; Isa 20:2 ; 1Kin 20:31-32 , Jer 48:37 . f. linen breeches of priests were to extend יְרֵכַיִם וְעַד מִמָּתְנַיִם Exod 28:42 (P); to be ׳עַלמָֿת Ezek 44:18 ; loins of slaves are girt with waistcloth, compare Job 12:18 (see also אֵזוֺר ). g. in General of the middle of the body, מָת ׳מֵי Ezek 47:4 (i.e. water reaching to the loins); so of the appearance of ׳י in Ezekiel's visions 1:27 (twice in verse); 8:2 (twice in verse). 2. a. loins as seat of strength, Deut 33:11 ; 1Kin 12:10 2Chr 10:10 ; מָתְנַיִם חַזֵּק Nahum 2:2 (|| כֹּחַ אַמֵּץ ); בְּמָתְנָיו כֹּחוֺ Job 40:16 (of hippopotamus); in combination with 1a (figurative) מ ׳בְּעוֺז חָֽגְרָה Prov 31:17 she girdeth her loins with strength , she puts on energy with her girdle; compare also מ ׳בְּשִׁבְרוֺן Ezek 21:11 sigh with breaking of loins , i.e. in entire collapse of strength; so וּמ ׳הַמְעַ֑ד תָּמִיד Psa 69:24 and make their loins continually to shake , make them totter; compare Ezek 29:7 (where read וְהִמְעַדְתָּ for וְהַעֲמַדְתָּ , see מָעַד ). b. as seat of keenest pain, due to grief or dread Nahum 2:11 ; Isa 21:3 (as in travail); so probably also Psa 66:11 (compare Bae; and see מוּעָקָה below עוק ).","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to be slender ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 2 5","keyReferences":["1Kgs 2 5","1Kgs 12 10","1Kgs 18 46","1Kgs 20 31","1Kgs 20 32","2Chr 10 10","2Kgs 1 8","2Kgs 4 29"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":47,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 2 5","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":5,"engli